| `tests.cache_dir` | string | `.pytest_cache`; absent, the same value from its loader row | checkout-relative directory, git-ignored, with no absolute path, empty, `.` or `..` part, symlink escape or tracked file | `scripts/changed_tests.py` through `scripts/config_loader.py`; `check_H` validates only relative spelling and checkout confinement, without git; the runner also requires git write safety | Holds pytest failure history for `make test-changed`; the runner passes its absolute checkout path through `-o cache_dir=...`. Both gitignore files ignore the default; a custom path needs both ignore entries. Removing the checkout removes the cache. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] tests.cache_dir = ".pytest_cache"` to stderr. | gate state: every other pytest recipe disables cacheprovider; this loop is never the gate | always |
